In the case that you have presented, the applicant would be permitted to work for a Canadian entity and provide professional services to the entities client. The only restriction being if hiring entity is substantially controlled (owned/controls/directs) by the
applicant as Professionals are not eligible to be self-employed in Canada under the NAFTA provisions.
In order to determine if an enterprise is substantially controlled, the following factors must be taken into account:
- whether the applicant has established the business;
- whether the applicant has primary, sole, or de facto control of the business;
- whether the applicant is the primary, sole, or de facto owner of the business;
- whether the applicant is the primary, sole, or de facto recipient of income of the business. Thanks
